    "article": "**Mets Make Statement in Philly, Take 4-1 Win**\n\nThe New York Mets made it two in a row with a dominant 4-1 victory over the Philadelphia Phillies, thanks in large part to the explosive bat of Francisco Alvarez. Alvarez was nearly unstoppable, crushing two home runs and driving in two runs on his way to a 2-for-3 night. On the mound, Christian Scott was equally impressive, tossing 5.2 scoreless innings with seven strikeouts and no walks. Scott's strong performance earned him the win, as the Mets' bullpen closed out the game in support.",
